    "rt.raw_json": { en: "Raw JSON feed" },
    "rt.loading": { en: "Loading the roots feed…" },
    "fl.lede": { en: "The black box behind every trade. Each decision the agent makes is sealed into a <b>SHA-256 hash-chained, signed append-only ledger</b> — inputs, reasoning, the voters that moved it, the risk-gate verdict, the intent policy that authorized it, the geometry and the outcome. Any edit, deletion or reorder breaks the chain. <b>Don't trust the P&amp;L — read the decision.</b>" },
    "fl.disc": { en: "Public decision ledger · percent, ratio and R-multiple only — <b>no dollar amounts</b> (prices shown are public market data). The cryptographic chain is verified by the engine; the window integrity below is re-derived in your own browser. This is evidence, not investment advice." },
    "sn.lede": { en: "A market-wide crowding radar. When the whole USDT-perp universe leans one way, funding runs hot, fresh leverage piles in and moves start correlating, a coordinated unwind — a <b>liquidation cascade</b> — gets more likely. The Sentinel reads those conditions across the market from <b>public data</b> and flags them. Heuristic reads, not a verdict and not investment advice." },
    "sn.disc": { en: "Public Bitget market data (funding, open interest, ΔOI, 24h direction) aggregated across the perp universe. Open interest shown is a <b>market</b> figure — a public fact, never anyone's account or P&amp;L. The gauge and flags are <b>heuristic crowding reads</b>, not predictions or signals; positioning can stay crowded for a long time. Build your own safety envelope in the <a href=\"/dashboard#agents\">app</a>." },
    "rt.intro": { en: "Every trading call and Arena paper trade is <a href=\"/dashboard#signals\">sealed the moment it's made</a>. At the end of each UTC day, all of that day's seals fold into <b>one Merkle root</b> — the single hash below. Copy a root anywhere you like (a tweet, a repo, a chain memo) and you hold an independent timestamp: nothing can be back-inserted into a day you mirrored without changing its root." },
    "rt.explain": { en: "<b>Construction</b> (mirrorable, verify it yourself): leaves are the day's seals (SHA-256 hex), deduped and sorted ascending; each parent is sha256 of the two child hex strings concatenated (UTF-8); an unpaired node is promoted unchanged; a single leaf is its own root. Every <a href=\"/dashboard#signals\">receipt</a> from a completed day replays its membership proof up to the day root <i>in your browser</i> on its verify page.<br> <b>What mirroring proves:</b> once a third party holds a day's root, that day's set of calls is frozen — the platform can't rewrite it without the mismatch showing. Roots for days with zero seals are omitted, never invented, and today's root is never published early. Not investment advice." },
    "ag.open_in_app": { en: "Open in app" },
